        "transcriptHtml": "<p class=\"transcript-note\">Automatic transcript. It may contain small recognition errors; the answer key is authoritative.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:01]</span> You will hear a conversation between two flatmates, Craig and Don, who are looking for a third person to share their flat. First, you have some time to look at questions 1 to 5. In the exam, you would have 25 seconds to look at the questions.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:21]</span> Pause the recording for 25 seconds now. Now we shall begin. You should answer the questions as you listen, because you will not hear the recording a second time.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:34]</span> Listen carefully and answer questions 1 to 5. Hi, Craig, been home long. Yeah, quite a time. Did anyone phone about renting the spare room?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:46]</span> Yeah, we&#x27;ve had three phone calls about it. Really? Yeah. Do you want to hear about them?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:52]</span> Sure. Right. The first one was called Phil Parrot. Uh-huh.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[00:58]</span> He&#x27;s a teacher. He&#x27;s just qualified and he teaches sports. Okay. Actually, I&#x27;m not sure about him.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:07]</span> He certainly sounded energetic, but he asked lots of questions about whether we smoked and what sort of food we cooked. Yeah. I mean, we don&#x27;t exactly live on pizza and chips and takeaways.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:20]</span> Well, not quite, but... But he might be a bit too health conscious to really fit in with the sort of life we lead. Yeah. And he asked a lot of questions about the room.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:31]</span> He said he needs a big room because he&#x27;s got lots of sports equipment. Well, that&#x27;s okay. The room&#x27;s quite big, but I&#x27;m not so sure about him. What about the second one?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:42]</span> He was called David Spencer. Spender? No, Spencer. C-E-R.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:49]</span> He works at Cooper Long. You know? The big company on Broad Street. He said he was a lawyer.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[01:56]</span> No. I&#x27;d have thought in that case he&#x27;d be earning enough to rent his own place. I wonder why he wants to share a flat. Well, he didn&#x27;t say.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:05]</span> He&#x27;s quite a bit older than us. He did say he&#x27;s just moved down here from the north of England. He seemed very quiet, actually. Maybe he wants to meet some new people.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:17]</span> I got the impression he was a hard-working kind of person who doesn&#x27;t go out all that much. Right. But he sounded okay. Oh, one thing, though.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:27]</span> He said he wouldn&#x27;t be staying in the flat at the weekends, so he wants to pay reduced costs for gas and electricity. Because he&#x27;s only here five days out of seven. Oh, I&#x27;m not sure about that. What do you think?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[02:42]</span> Well, I suppose it&#x27;s fair, but it all sounds a bit complicated. Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at question six to ten. In the exam, you would have twenty-five seconds to look at the questions. Pause the recording for twenty-five seconds now.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:05]</span> Now listen and answer questions six to ten. Anyway, there was a third person, Leo Norris. Yes? He&#x27;s an engineer.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:21]</span> Oh, yeah. And he&#x27;s about our age. Right. What did he sound like?</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:26]</span> Well, actually, he was really funny. I couldn&#x27;t stop laughing when I was talking to him. He said he was very lazy and never got up until noon at weekends, and I said that wouldn&#x27;t be a problem here. No, certainly not.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:41]</span> But actually, I suspect he was joking when he said he was lazy. I think he lives life as it comes. He&#x27;s certainly not competitive or stressed, but he likes cycling and things like that. He sounds like an outdoor type.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[03:55]</span> Anyway, I thought he sounded as if he&#x27;d fit in. He wanted to check if there was somewhere safe for his bicycle. That&#x27;s not a problem. No.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:03]</span> He can leave it in the garage with my car. So did you get his contact details? Yes. He left his mobile number.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:11]</span> It&#x27;s O, 777-687-2433. And does he want to move in straight away? Well, he&#x27;s paid his rent in his present place up to the 31st of September. But he said that if possible, he&#x27;d like to move in a bit before then.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:30]</span> He said the 28th of September. And he was okay about the rent? Yeah. He said it was fine.</p><p><span class=\"ts\">[04:37]</span> Right. So shall we give him a ring and see if he wants to come around? Now turn to section two.</p>"
